# Runtime contract violation (port of src/tests/contracts-runtime-violation.test.ts):
# the program compiles cleanly and PANICS at run time; `build run` propagates
# that as rc=1 under BOTH compilers — the rc parity is the assertion. The
# panic message ("requires failed: ..."/"ensures failed: ...") is byte-
# identical across compilers (probe-verified) but rides stderr with build
# chatter the two binaries word differently, hence stdout=ignore (the
# documented escape).
# stdout_keep_match (P2.5 step 15): this case previously used stdout=ignore,
# which ANY failure satisfied. The kept substring is the probe-verified
# SHARED diagnostic - both compilers must emit it, so the case asserts THE
# failure, not just A failure.
stdout_keep_match=ensures failed:.*
timeout=300
